      "sequence_position": 4,
      "problem": "Compute $P(X<1)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{8}{x}^{2},\\, & 0\\le x\\le 2, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a\\le X<b)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)$ is identical to zero for all $x<0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<1) & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{3}{8}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{8}{x}^{3}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}[1-0] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
